WEBVTT

00:07.620 --> 00:09.850
Sorry, Bel, can I come in for a sec?

00:11.490 --> 00:12.990
Suzu-sis!

00:13.300 --> 00:16.840
Emilia? Have you been at the Devil's Castle?

00:16.840 --> 00:20.630
Yes. Can I leave Alas Ramus 
with you for a bit?

00:20.630 --> 00:22.270
Is something wrong?

00:22.950 --> 00:24.550
I'll be quick.

00:28.440 --> 00:30.190
Denied!

00:30.530 --> 00:33.400
What's wrong with Alas Ramus sleeping over?!

00:33.400 --> 00:35.760
There's no way I'd allow that!

00:36.080 --> 00:38.110
And you call yourself her mother?!

00:38.110 --> 00:41.600
Simply ignoring a child's 
wish to be with her father

00:41.600 --> 00:45.140
is too barbaric and cruel for any 
"hero"—nay, for any <i>person</i>!

00:45.140 --> 00:47.400
<i>You're</i> the barbaric and cruel ones.

00:47.840 --> 00:52.540
You don't even have futons. You want to 
make Alas Ramus sleep on the hard floor?!

00:54.220 --> 00:58.730
If you really want me to let Alas 
Ramus sleep here, at least buy a futon.

00:59.060 --> 01:01.910
You've got perfectly 
good storage space for it.

01:01.910 --> 01:06.000
I've given up on that closet. 
That's where we store Urushihara.

01:06.000 --> 01:08.420
Are you saying I'm junk to be
thrown in the closet?

01:08.420 --> 01:11.490
Forget the top shelf. If you 
organize the bottom a bit,

01:11.490 --> 01:13.770
you can fit a futon down there.

01:13.770 --> 01:18.440
Emilia, could you not agree with them
 about me being stored on this shelf?

01:20.230 --> 01:25.180
I hate to say this, but I actually want to take

01:25.520 --> 01:28.750
the stuff from this Devil's Castle 
with me when I go back to Ente Isla.

01:28.750 --> 01:31.820
We should be able to use 
the microwave and the fridge there

01:31.820 --> 01:33.320
if we make them magic-powered.

01:33.320 --> 01:37.960
I've got the same plan. But you 
could bring futons too, right?

01:37.960 --> 01:40.420
Nope, no can do.

01:40.800 --> 01:44.050
Think about it! We're demons.

01:44.050 --> 01:46.770
What good would human-sized futons be?

01:51.000 --> 01:52.210
Don't laugh!

01:52.210 --> 01:55.470
Anyway, we can't use futons over there.

01:55.470 --> 01:57.430
And frankly, we don't have the money.

01:57.430 --> 02:02.240
You've been in Japan for a year now. 
What did you do in the winter?

02:02.850 --> 02:05.720
We wore multiple layers
and slept under the kotatsu.

02:06.960 --> 02:11.980
Maybe I don't have to take you down. 
You can just freeze to death this winter.

02:12.360 --> 02:16.190
All right, fine. I don't care 
what happens to you guys,

02:16.190 --> 02:18.880
but Alas Ramus is important to me.

02:18.880 --> 02:22.200
I'll contribute half the money for her futon.

02:22.200 --> 02:23.990
We'll shop for one together, got it?

02:25.060 --> 02:26.380
For real?!

02:45.810 --> 02:47.890
<b>The Devil is a Part-Timer! Season 2</b>

03:57.000 --> 04:01.970
m 370 218 l 609 218 609 245 370 245

03:58.550 --> 04:01.970
<b>The Devil and the Hero Go Futon Shopping</b>

03:58.550 --> 04:01.970
<b>The Devil and the Hero Go Futon Shopping</b>

03:59.510 --> 04:02.950
Why did I say I'd go shopping with him?

04:02.950 --> 04:04.260
Is something wrong?

04:04.260 --> 04:09.390
Say, where could I buy a kid's futon?

04:09.390 --> 04:11.610
Huh? Why do you want one?

04:11.610 --> 04:16.580
Er, r-remember that relative 
of Maou's I told you about?

04:16.580 --> 04:19.650
The girl who mistook you for her mother?

04:20.010 --> 04:25.260
Right, her. She comes to visit me, 
and even sleeps over sometimes...

04:25.260 --> 04:30.940
What for? You don't mean Mister Maou 
is making you babysit her, do you?

04:30.940 --> 04:32.660
It's not like that.

04:32.660 --> 04:37.920
Then why? If he's pulling anything 
funny here, I'll tear him a new one for you.

04:37.920 --> 04:40.800
I'll even get you a lawyer 
through my parents' business.

04:40.800 --> 04:45.460
Calm down, Rika. It's not 
like Maou's a child neglecter.

04:45.870 --> 04:50.450
It's just, you know, I guess 
kids her age miss their moms.

04:50.450 --> 04:53.920
And however I may feel 
about Maou, I do like her.

04:53.920 --> 04:58.060
I'm just letting her stay with me 
when she really needs to, I guess.

04:58.060 --> 05:01.610
Huh. Well, it's weird, but...

05:01.610 --> 05:04.960
I've looked at some online shops,

05:04.960 --> 05:08.570
but it's for a child, so I want to 
see how it feels to the touch, you know?

05:08.950 --> 05:12.580
Oh! Then I know where you can go.

05:13.140 --> 05:18.170
I appreciate her paying half, 
but where do we even buy a futon?

05:18.820 --> 05:21.440
Is something wrong, Mister Maou?

05:21.440 --> 05:22.340
Nah.

05:23.010 --> 05:27.760
<i>I don't wanna ask Chi. But asking 
the others isn't much better...</i>

05:27.760 --> 05:29.970
Oh, hi, Maa and Chi!

05:30.250 --> 05:33.280
Here, a present from my 
summer vacation with friends.

05:33.280 --> 05:35.600
Aw, you shouldn't have.

05:35.600 --> 05:36.580
Here's yours, Chi.

05:36.580 --> 05:38.100
Thank you!

05:40.180 --> 05:41.230
Crocodile curry?!

05:41.230 --> 05:43.610
It's surprisingly tasty!

05:43.610 --> 05:47.540
Where did you guys go? Not the Amazon, right?

05:48.900 --> 05:50.740
What's your guess?

05:50.740 --> 05:53.240
<b>Received Message</b>

05:50.740 --> 05:53.240
<b>Emi</b>

05:50.740 --> 05:53.240
<b>The futon</b>

05:50.740 --> 05:53.240
<b>We're going to Seiseki Sakuragaoka!
Tell me what day you're free.</b>

05:53.840 --> 05:56.120
Futon shopping at Seiseki Sakuragaoka?

05:56.120 --> 05:57.350
Yeah.

05:57.350 --> 06:01.510
She says it has lots of stores, and we 
can check out the futons before we buy.

06:01.510 --> 06:05.510
Neither of us have shifts the day 
after tomorrow, so we'll go buy it then.

06:05.980 --> 06:10.610
She's right—it's got lots of big shopping 
centers connected to the train station.

06:10.610 --> 06:14.520
That's a relief, isn't it? 
I was worried last night.

06:14.830 --> 06:17.020
Sorry for dragging you into it.

06:17.650 --> 06:19.270
What's that?

06:19.270 --> 06:22.770
Oh, it's from one of my coworkers.

06:22.770 --> 06:24.400
Apparently it's got crocodile meat—

06:24.400 --> 06:25.900
Crocodile meat?!

06:26.900 --> 06:29.810
I wonder what crocodile meat tastes like...

06:29.810 --> 06:33.120
I-If you're that curious, you can have it.

06:33.120 --> 06:34.160
Really?!

06:34.160 --> 06:39.390
Sure. It's only one serving, so we 
can't really split it three ways anyway.

06:39.960 --> 06:42.290
Just tell us how you liked it.

06:42.290 --> 06:45.540
Sire, our food reserves are precious.

06:45.540 --> 06:49.950
What's the harm? We'll owe her 
after we get a futon anyway.

06:51.140 --> 06:52.760
Have you forgotten, Ashiya?

06:53.210 --> 06:55.770
Now that Alas Ramus is fused with the sword,

06:55.770 --> 06:58.560
she has to stay within a certain radius of Emi.

06:58.560 --> 07:03.580
Ah, yes. About the distance between 
two train stations, as I recall?

07:03.580 --> 07:07.510
Yep. Which means that 
if Alas Ramus stays with us,

07:07.510 --> 07:10.660
Emi can't go back to her place in Eifukucho.

07:10.660 --> 07:15.530
You mean the best course is to have 
Alciel and Lucifer sleep in my apartment,

07:15.530 --> 07:17.120
like when Gabriel came?

07:17.120 --> 07:20.580
What? Can't I stay in the closet?

07:20.580 --> 07:23.030
So after all that, you're gonna 
voluntarily store yourself?

07:24.570 --> 07:28.550
Anyway, we're bound to 
inconvenience you one way or another.

07:28.550 --> 07:31.080
So take the crocodile curry.

07:31.080 --> 07:33.840
I bet you'll enjoy taking a break 
from udon once in a while.

07:39.740 --> 07:42.170
I can't just <i>not</i> eat udon.

07:48.440 --> 07:51.590
And now, I feast.

07:57.200 --> 08:00.070
Now, Alas Ramus, be good.

08:00.070 --> 08:01.330
'Kay!

08:01.330 --> 08:02.830
What's that paper?

08:02.830 --> 08:05.790
Ashiya said to buy these 
if I find them cheap.

08:06.600 --> 08:12.220
One bag of onions, shirodashi, 
natto, dish soap refill...

08:12.580 --> 08:16.270
Are these worth riding a train 
for just to get them cheaper?

08:16.270 --> 08:17.720
Probably not.

08:19.720 --> 08:21.800
Papa! Magronals!

08:21.800 --> 08:23.630
Yep, that's right.

08:23.630 --> 08:26.150
She's been begging to eat there lately.

08:26.150 --> 08:28.860
I keep telling her she's too young.

08:28.860 --> 08:30.110
Really?

08:30.110 --> 08:32.740
She says it "smells like Papa."

08:36.280 --> 08:39.100
Hey, are you okay, Alas Ramus?

08:39.450 --> 08:41.380
I'm so sorry, everyone.

08:45.200 --> 08:46.650
Oh, jeez.

08:51.260 --> 08:54.960
How come she can go ten rounds 
with an archangel

08:54.960 --> 08:57.260
but bumping her forehead makes her cry?

08:57.260 --> 08:58.970
No idea.

08:58.970 --> 09:01.990
Parenting is a series of surprises, huh?

09:01.990 --> 09:05.070
Yeah, though I think we're lucky 
that she can't get lost.

09:08.990 --> 09:09.990
What's wrong?

09:12.210 --> 09:16.230
We're acting like we're really married!

09:19.090 --> 09:23.040
All right, this should 
be enough storage space.

09:23.040 --> 09:27.100
Hey, are we really gonna sleep at Bel's?

09:27.100 --> 09:31.330
I don't want to either, but if
 Alas Ramus wishes it, we must.

09:31.330 --> 09:32.720
Wow, you're serious.

09:32.720 --> 09:35.170
But I can just stay here, right?

09:35.170 --> 09:37.610
Closet junk doesn't get a vote.

09:37.610 --> 09:39.660
It's up to Emilia.

09:39.660 --> 09:44.180
Won't this be a burden 
to Bel, not just Emilia?

09:44.180 --> 09:46.650
I don't think so...

09:46.650 --> 09:49.760
Still, we don't want an argument
at the last minute.

09:49.760 --> 09:51.890
I'll talk to her now, just to make sure.

10:01.700 --> 10:02.750
She's not here?

10:06.230 --> 10:08.110
Aw, she's so cute!

10:08.110 --> 10:12.410
She has her mother's eyes 
and her father's mouth!

10:15.860 --> 10:17.830
Get it together, would you?

10:18.410 --> 10:21.860
What might you be looking for today?

10:21.860 --> 10:25.600
U-Um, we'd like a futon she can use.

10:25.600 --> 10:30.670
Oh, I see. Have you been 
using a bassinet so far?

10:30.670 --> 10:32.860
No, she co-sleeps with her mother.

10:33.480 --> 10:37.240
Hey! Stop freezing every time 
you think "family"!

10:38.970 --> 10:41.740
Well, what about these?

10:42.100 --> 10:44.140
They have stuffed animals attached?

10:44.140 --> 10:48.370
Yes, so that children can 
hug them as they fall asleep.

10:48.710 --> 10:52.990
The filling in this comforter can 
be adjusted as the seasons change.

10:52.990 --> 10:57.510
The set also comes with a pillow 
and blanket, for a total of ¥29,800.

10:57.510 --> 10:58.760
<i>Twenty...</i>

10:58.760 --> 11:04.760
This one is ¥45,800, and comes with 
both a winter and a summer comforter.

11:04.760 --> 11:06.080
<i>Forty...!</i>

11:08.270 --> 11:10.620
She doesn't answer no matter 
how many times I knock.

11:10.620 --> 11:14.600
Maybe she ran away. Because she 
doesn't want us to sleep over.

11:14.600 --> 11:16.110
That's ridiculous.

11:16.110 --> 11:20.150
She's the one who suggested we 
sleep there in the first place.

11:20.460 --> 11:23.570
What if she changed her mind later?

11:24.140 --> 11:29.790
Oh hey, she came and left something here 
yesterday while you were out shopping.

11:32.230 --> 11:35.390
I don't want this anymore. You take it.

11:36.490 --> 11:38.180
Why didn't you tell me earlier?!

11:41.430 --> 11:43.430
U-Udon?!

11:43.430 --> 11:47.700
Wh-What does this mean? 
Bel, giving up her udon?

11:51.440 --> 11:54.550
Please, browse as much as you like.

11:54.550 --> 11:55.500
Thanks.

11:57.130 --> 12:00.110
It's all extremes, you know?

12:00.110 --> 12:03.490
At first I was like, over 
¥40,000 is just crazy...

12:03.490 --> 12:06.570
But then the next store is 
selling them for ¥3,000?

12:06.570 --> 12:10.690
The ¥3,000 ones are "nap sets" 
for day care, remember?

12:10.690 --> 12:14.710
They're fundamentally different from 
the futons designed for a good night's sleep.

12:15.060 --> 12:18.710
The first price we saw was so steep, 
I can't tell what's reasonable.

12:19.090 --> 12:23.780
Going too expensive is a problem, 
but I'd be worried if we went too cheap.

12:25.220 --> 12:27.110
What, Papa?

12:27.720 --> 12:31.480
And I want to get something 
good for Alas Ramus.

12:34.090 --> 12:37.580
Hey, Alas Ramus, there's 
a staircase coming up.

12:37.580 --> 12:39.280
Hold on to Mama, okay?

12:39.280 --> 12:40.110
'Kay!

12:40.110 --> 12:41.610
Wait, wha—

12:41.610 --> 12:43.120
Whee!

12:48.350 --> 12:51.530
Come on, Emi, get used to this already.

12:51.530 --> 12:53.750
You okay, Mama?

12:56.770 --> 13:01.210
Well, it looks like Mama's tired, 
so let's break for lunch.

13:01.210 --> 13:02.380
'Kay!

13:05.280 --> 13:07.260
Is it that tough a choice?

13:07.260 --> 13:09.220
What's wrong, Mama?

13:09.220 --> 13:11.090
Mama's okay.

13:11.090 --> 13:17.450
What's tough is deciding whether I should 
prioritize "Hero" or "Mama," that's all.

13:17.900 --> 13:20.710
Let's see, where can Alas Ramus eat...

13:21.240 --> 13:25.570
I'm sorry. Both of my priorities 
work pretty much the same, so...

13:25.570 --> 13:27.390
Oh, how about soba?

13:27.390 --> 13:29.150
Soba!

13:29.150 --> 13:32.560
I don't need you to feel sorry for me.

13:32.560 --> 13:36.150
That soba place is expensive. 
The noodles come with tempura.

13:36.150 --> 13:38.000
Tempura!

13:38.000 --> 13:39.510
What do you mean?

13:39.510 --> 13:41.100
Tempura, eh?

13:42.050 --> 13:44.380
What do you think I mean?

13:45.360 --> 13:49.280
Wait, can you even afford to eat out?

13:49.280 --> 13:54.790
I do have <i>some</i> money. I get some 
fun money from each month's pay,

13:54.790 --> 13:58.590
and on my working days Ashiya 
gives me a ¥300 allowance.

13:58.590 --> 14:01.370
But is that what we were talking about?

14:01.370 --> 14:03.640
We're talking about lunch.

14:03.640 --> 14:07.820
No, I feel like we were talking 
about something a bit more serious...

14:07.820 --> 14:10.000
If you prioritized "Papa" over "the Devil,"

14:10.000 --> 14:13.900
and traded world conquest 
for living your life out in Japan,

14:13.900 --> 14:15.580
<i>my</i> life would be easy.

14:25.450 --> 14:26.430
So...

14:26.430 --> 14:27.260
What?

14:27.680 --> 14:31.750
The MgRonald's here should give us 
fries without salt if we ask.

14:31.750 --> 14:33.350
Magronals!

14:33.350 --> 14:35.430
You want some, right?

14:35.430 --> 14:37.640
Why don't we let her have just a few?

14:37.640 --> 14:39.740
Where's this coming from?

14:39.740 --> 14:43.110
And how about we get takeout 
and go eat over there?

14:43.110 --> 14:46.110
<b>Ichinomiya Park</b>

14:43.110 --> 14:46.110
<b>Tama River</b>

14:43.610 --> 14:44.980
Let's have a picnic.

14:47.010 --> 14:49.170
Bel, giving up her udon?

14:49.850 --> 14:52.310
Could she have gone on a long trip?

14:52.310 --> 14:54.820
Maybe she went to Udon World.

14:54.820 --> 14:57.370
Udon World? Does Japan have such a land?!

14:58.490 --> 15:04.330
His Majesty has gone to buy a futon 
so he can look forward to family time,

15:04.330 --> 15:07.130
but if Bel doesn't come back tonight...

15:07.790 --> 15:09.760
the sleepover can't happen!

15:10.390 --> 15:17.140
This place has a ton of empty apartments. 
Why not stay in one of those?

15:17.140 --> 15:19.640
That's right! We could ask 
the landlady's permiss—

15:23.590 --> 15:26.150
It's no use. I can't.

15:27.930 --> 15:32.530
I can't possibly negotiate with that landlady!

15:38.040 --> 15:40.510
Wow, it's a big park!

15:42.510 --> 15:44.720
Don't trip, Alas Ramus!

15:48.860 --> 15:50.520
Up you go.

15:50.930 --> 15:52.810
Sit down. You're gonna eat, right?

15:52.810 --> 15:53.610
Yeah.

15:58.600 --> 16:00.430
Magronals!

16:00.820 --> 16:04.050
Now, what do we do before we eat?

16:04.050 --> 16:07.240
Fank you for the food!

16:07.240 --> 16:10.010
Time to clean off your hands, Alas Ramus.

16:13.460 --> 16:14.460
Here.

16:19.440 --> 16:20.690
Here, tea.

16:28.110 --> 16:29.210
It's good.

16:29.210 --> 16:32.870
Right? They sell it at 
the 100-yen shop. It's a fave.

16:35.250 --> 16:38.390
Alas Ramus, I bet those fries 
are making you thirsty.

16:38.390 --> 16:39.470
Drink some tea.

16:41.860 --> 16:42.970
'Kay!

16:44.680 --> 16:47.430
You two really look like family doing that.

16:47.960 --> 16:50.180
I hope I get used to it.

16:51.220 --> 16:55.590
You're usually pretty at home 
in Mom Mode yourself.

16:55.590 --> 16:58.570
W-Well, I...

16:59.120 --> 17:04.470
I wonder how long we'll be able to 
be with Alas Ramus like this...

17:05.420 --> 17:06.560
Satan...

17:06.560 --> 17:08.520
Mama! Rice!

17:09.130 --> 17:10.380
Oh, right.

17:11.050 --> 17:11.880
Here.

17:14.520 --> 17:17.670
Right for the pickled radish, huh?
You're a real grown-up!

17:21.320 --> 17:25.250
But you know, freezing up 
thinking about that won't help.

17:26.250 --> 17:29.870
You're not planning to kill me 
with the sacred sword for now,

17:29.870 --> 17:32.150
so thinking about it's a waste of time.

17:32.490 --> 17:37.090
That doesn't mean 
I've given up on taking you down...

17:37.090 --> 17:39.030
No need to be so defensive.

17:39.030 --> 17:42.090
I'm not planning to take advantage 
of that to do anything bad.

17:42.490 --> 17:44.910
Ack, the bonito is falling out!

17:45.410 --> 17:47.590
Hey, Emi, you have chopsticks, right?

17:47.590 --> 17:49.350
And I'll get a wet wipe...

17:49.350 --> 17:52.190
One second. Here you go, Alas Ramus...

17:53.490 --> 17:58.430
Anyway, the Devil and the Hero are 
irrelevant while we're doing this, huh?

18:12.910 --> 18:14.800
Nice weather today.

18:19.480 --> 18:21.450
There's no more time to spare.

18:22.050 --> 18:25.000
Should we use the internet 
café by the station?

18:25.000 --> 18:30.330
But overnight packages for Urushihara 
and I would be ¥1,980 times two!

18:30.330 --> 18:33.330
That would greatly strain 
this month's finances.

18:33.330 --> 18:35.390
So do we sleep outside in the park?!

18:35.390 --> 18:38.520
No, that won't work. Me alone is one thing,

18:38.520 --> 18:42.600
but with Urushihara, people might report us 
to the police as suspicious persons!

18:42.600 --> 18:45.990
Wait, I know who I can 
consult at times like this.

19:01.610 --> 19:04.020
How dare you? How dare you?

19:04.020 --> 19:06.240
Hmm? What's wrong?

19:06.240 --> 19:09.750
How dare you sleep 
against me the whole ride?!

19:09.750 --> 19:11.480
F-For real?

19:11.480 --> 19:13.380
Don't play dumb!

19:13.380 --> 19:15.450
An old lady got on at 
Sakurajosui and cooed at me.

19:15.450 --> 19:17.910
"What a sweet couple!"

19:17.910 --> 19:21.010
You owe me for that humiliation!

19:21.450 --> 19:23.710
Mister Maou? Miss Yusa?

19:23.710 --> 19:25.590
Ch-Chi?!

19:25.590 --> 19:28.390
What are you two doing here?

19:28.390 --> 19:32.530
Well, you see, we had some shopping...

19:34.210 --> 19:37.880
Chi-sis, mornin'.

19:37.880 --> 19:42.660
Good morning, Alas Ramus. 
Did you go somewhere today?

19:42.660 --> 19:45.660
Picnic with Papa and Mama.

19:45.660 --> 19:48.580
Oh, a pic—huh?

19:49.540 --> 19:52.420
I'm gonna sleep with Mama and Papa tonight!

19:52.420 --> 19:55.690
What? With Mister Maou and Miss Yusa?

19:55.690 --> 19:58.730
No, Chiho, it's not like that!

19:58.730 --> 20:02.490
Calm down, Chi! You know Emi 
and I wouldn't sleep together!

20:02.490 --> 20:04.930
Gonna buy a futon.

20:04.930 --> 20:06.940
Fu...Futon!

20:09.010 --> 20:12.830
Are you really going to be f-f-family?

20:12.830 --> 20:15.160
M-Miss Yusa, moving to <i>that</i> apartment?!

20:17.090 --> 20:17.610
Chi!

20:17.690 --> 20:19.820
Chiho, get a grip!

20:19.820 --> 20:22.080
As if I'd sleep with <i>her</i>!

20:22.080 --> 20:24.070
I certainly wouldn't sleep with <i>him</i>!

20:24.070 --> 20:29.270
B-But if you two have decided, then I won't...

20:29.950 --> 20:33.570
Papa, Mama, no fighting!

20:34.740 --> 20:36.960
D-Don't cry, Alas Ramus!

20:36.960 --> 20:38.960
We're not fighting, okay?

20:38.960 --> 20:41.840
Your Majesty! And Emilia and Miss Sasaki...

20:41.840 --> 20:44.000
What's all this commotion?

20:46.970 --> 20:51.720
I see, so the futon is 
for Alas Ramus to sleep over.

20:51.720 --> 20:53.600
I told you so.

20:53.600 --> 20:57.890
Well, I was surprised. You three 
really looked like family.

20:57.890 --> 20:59.170
Don't go there.

20:57.890 --> 20:59.170
Please don't go there.

20:59.170 --> 21:00.860
You're on the same wavelength.

21:00.860 --> 21:05.800
Well, Sire? What about the futon mission?

21:05.800 --> 21:10.630
Actually, I invited Emi over so 
we could ask your advice about it.

21:10.630 --> 21:13.920
I assume it's expensive, then.

21:13.920 --> 21:16.780
Well, not having one today is for the best.

21:16.780 --> 21:20.500
Oh hey, Ashiya, who were 
you on the phone with?

21:20.500 --> 21:24.800
We've lost contact with Bel, I'm afraid,

21:24.800 --> 21:27.880
so I called Miss Suzuki 
for advice on the matter.

21:27.880 --> 21:28.960
Bel?

21:30.900 --> 21:33.040
Bel! Hello, Bel?!

21:34.520 --> 21:37.410
Perhaps she really left for Udon World...

21:39.430 --> 21:40.450
Shh!

21:40.930 --> 21:43.060
Miss Suzuno, are you there?

21:44.680 --> 21:45.970
I'm coming in!

21:51.980 --> 21:54.010
Miss Suzuno?

21:54.010 --> 21:56.290
What on earth happened?

22:11.380 --> 22:15.680
Suzuno, did you use that 
crocodile curry to make curry udon?

22:15.680 --> 22:19.540
Yes. And then when I ate it,

22:19.540 --> 22:22.600
it splashed on my favorite kimono!

22:24.150 --> 22:28.360
And the shock made you decide 
not to eat udon for a while?

22:29.110 --> 22:31.700
Next time call me, and I'll tell 
you how to get the stains out.

22:31.700 --> 22:34.560
How could I tell others 
something so pathetic?!

22:34.560 --> 22:36.480
But it's not a big deal, so—

22:36.480 --> 22:41.340
Don't say that! I was really shocked!

22:41.340 --> 22:43.800
I guess the path to sleepovers 
will be steep, huh?

22:43.800 --> 22:44.900
Indeed.

22:48.140 --> 22:52.600
That's why we're going back 
to buy the futon next week.

22:54.930 --> 22:56.120
What's wrong?

22:56.120 --> 23:00.280
I'm startin' not to know m'self.

23:00.600 --> 23:01.480
Huh?

23:02.090 --> 23:08.990
I wonder if people always felt this 
impatient in the era before mobile phones.

23:12.580 --> 23:15.370
I honestly don't know anymore.

23:15.370 --> 23:17.750
Should I defeat the Devil or not?

23:18.200 --> 23:22.250
Here's what I've heard that married 
couples say when they're struggling:

23:22.710 --> 23:26.000
"I'm going to stay with 
my parents for a while."

23:26.000 --> 23:27.680
We're not married!

23:29.170 --> 23:30.800
But actually...

23:32.840 --> 23:38.630
Maybe visiting Ente Isla and sorting out 
my feelings for a bit isn't such a bad idea.
